  {
    "label": "figure_title",
    "text": "Table 1. Key parameters and main simulation results. zini denotes the starting redshift of the simulation, while zfinal corresponds to the final saved snapshot. Neff denotes the equivalent uniform particle resolution for the initial box of size L = 2 cMpc/h. For the full-box simulations, this corresponds to the actual particle resolution, whereas for the refined-region ('_2sigzoom') simulations it represents the uniform-box resolution that would give the same particle mass as in the highest-resolution region. er denotes the fraction of the BH feedback energy thermally coupled to the surrounding gas, while (fedd) ≡ (M•/Medd) gives the time-averaged Eddington ratio between zini and zfinal. The (co-moving) softening lengths for (particle) DM, gas, and stellar particles are given by eDm, egas, and e*, respectively. Mh,pí is the mass of the halo chosen to host the PBH, at the last snapshot of the simulation.",
